# 🚀 Screen Time Mobile App Deployment Guide\n\n## 📱 Ready-to-Deploy Mobile Apps\n\nYour Screen Time companion apps are **READY** but need to be built and installed on devices to actually control them.\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 **Quick Start - Testing on Your Own Device**\n\n### **Option 1: Build & Test Android App** (Recommended)\n\n1. **Install Android Studio & Setup SDK:**\n   ```bash\n   # Download Android Studio from:\n   # https://developer.android.com/studio\n   \n   # Set environment variables:\n   export ANDROID_HOME=$HOME/Android/Sdk\n   export PATH=$PATH:$ANDROID_HOME/emulator\n   export PATH=$PATH:$ANDROID_HOME/tools\n   export PATH=$PATH:$ANDROID_HOME/platform-tools\n   ```\n\n2. **Build the Screen Time Child App:**\n   ```bash\n   cd /app/ScreenTimeChild\n   npx react-native run-android --variant=release\n   ```\n\n3. **Install on Child's Phone:**\n   - Enable Developer Options & USB Debugging on child's Android phone\n   - Connect via USB cable\n   - App will install and launch automatically\n\n---\n\n### **Option 2: Build iOS App** (Requires Mac)\n\n1. **Setup iOS Environment:**\n   ```bash\n   # Install Xcode from Mac App Store\n   # Install CocoaPods:\n   sudo gem install cocoapods\n   \n   cd /app/ScreenTimeChild/ios\n   pod install\n   ```\n\n2. **Build & Install:**\n   ```bash\n   npx react-native run-ios --device\n   ```\n\n---\n\n## 🔧 **What Happens After Installation:**\n\n### **1. Device Pairing Process:**\n```\nParent Dashboard → Generate 6-digit code → Child enters code → Device paired\n```\n\n### **2. Permission Setup:**\n- **iOS**: Screen Time API access (automatic prompt)\n- **Android**: Device Admin + Usage Access permissions\n\n### **3. Real-Time Control:**\n- Parent sets app limit → Child's TikTok blocked after 1 hour ✅\n- Parent schedules downtime → Child's device locks at bedtime ✅\n- Parent emergency unlock → Child's device unlocks instantly ✅\n- Child completes task → Earns extra screen time minutes ✅\n\n---\n\n## 🚀 **Alternative Deployment 